# oracle: pair lubricateU/poly (mu 1.5, flaglog 1, cutinner 2.01, cutoff 2.5, gdot 0.01, flagHI 1, flagVF 1, newton off) on 64 polydisperse spheres (diameters 2.0 and 1.6, half of each type) on a 4x4x4 lattice of spacing 2.4 with random displacements, fix nve/noforce, 20 steps
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 1.4e-9, atoms 1.1e-9.
# Not at rounding level: the CG of this style is ill-conditioned at step 7 (native 354 iterations, engine 615); its result depends on the summation order of the full neighbor list, which the engine does not reproduce (reversing the list order moves the step-7 atom error from 7e-10 to 3.2e-10).
# native: installed lmp (b332f28)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      sphere
boundary        p p p
newton          off
lattice         sc 0.072338
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
displace_atoms  all random 0.1 0.1 0.1 4711 units box
group           half id 1:32
set             group half type 2
set             type 1 diameter 2.0
set             type 1 mass 4.18879
set             type 2 diameter 1.6
set             type 2 mass 2.14
velocity        all create 0.5 87287 loop geom
comm_modify     vel yes
pair_style      lubricateU/poly 1.5 1 2.01 2.5 0.01 1 1
pair_coeff      * *
fix             1 all nve/noforce
timestep        0.05
thermo_style    custom step temp press atoms
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             20
